     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":2,\"rationale\":\"The stages run in a fixed chain, so exfiltration is impossible exactly when every technique for at least one stage is blocked. Recon (internal_reconnaissance) has no blocking control, so it cannot be cut. Every other stage has two techniques, and no single control blocks both techniques of any stage, so one control is never enough. Two controls are sufficient: for example, patch_struts (or waf) plus email_filtering (or security_awareness) blocks both foothold techniques. The same works with credential_vaulting+edr, network_segmentation+vpn_mfa, db_access_control+replica_isolation, or dns_monitoring+proxy_tls_inspection. The minimum is 2.\"}"
    }
